==Strategy==
==='''Chapter 1'''===
This stage is trivial as the aliens are unbuffed, meaning the only threats are the angels. Because of this, [[Rocker Cat (Rare Cat)|Ramen Cat]] can basically do this stage by himself, as he has 71k to 89k effective health against angels. After this, just back it up with any stackable attacker such as [[Mer-Cat (Rare Cat)|Cameraman Cat]], [[Salon Cat (Rare Cat)|Cyborg Cat]], or any of the [[Lizard Cat (Normal Cat)|Dragon Cat]] or [[Gross Cat (Normal Cat)|Macho Leg Cat]] variants.

==='''Chapter 2'''===
You can use a similar strategy to the one used in  chapter 1, as there is almost no diffrence besides the UltraBaaBaa. Make sure to bring Kitty of Liberty or another barrier breaker to deal with UltraBaaBaa. Mistress Celeboodle has a 800% buff, but this doesn't prevent your units from easily killing her, so she is not a threat.

==='''Chapter 3'''===
This stage can be done with minimal effort, as the actual threat appears on base hit, meaning you have time to save money and deploy your heavy attackers. You can use [[Rocker Cat (Rare Cat)|Ramen Cat]] to tank damage from the angel peons, as his resistance to angels allows him to tank an insane amount of hits from all angel peons. You can also use high damage dealers such as [[Bahamut Cat (Special Cat)|Awakened Bahamut Cat]] to quickly kill the [[Mesocosmocyclone]] and deal high damage to the other peons, allowing your units to destroy the base.

